# On-demand surface-roughness (Ra) prediction for a single frame.
#
# Correctly a SERVICE, by this workspace's own rule (duration / cancellability /
# is there a result): inference is sub-second, there is nothing to cancel, and
# the whole point is the returned number. Compare CaptureImages.srv, which is a
# service for the same three reasons.
#
# Served by inference_node, which owns the ONNX session the way
# basler_camera_node owns the camera: loaded and warmed up once at startup, so
# callers pay no load cost and several consumers share one resident copy. A UI
# must call this rather than loading a model of its own — two copies is ~250 MB
# of duplicated RAM and two answers that drift apart the moment the paths do.
#
# ⚠️ PREPROCESSING IS CenterCrop(900, 900), NOT Resize.
# These graphs take a fixed 900x900 input and their first act is to cut it into
# a 3x3 grid of 300x300 tiles fed to Conv3d (visible in the exported graph as
# Slice/Transpose into 3D convolutions). The tiles are meant to be NATIVE Basler
# pixels. The camera delivers 5472x3648, so resizing to 900x900 makes each tile
# cover ~6x the surface at ~1/6 the detail, and the texture scale a roughness
# model reads is destroyed — while it still returns a confident-looking number.
#
# The scan pipeline resized until 2026-08-12 and now centre-crops through the
# same RaPredictor, so the two paths cannot disagree. Ra values recorded before
# that date came out of the resize transform and are NOT comparable with new
# ones. See CLAUDE.md.

# Frame to score, bgr8. Take it straight from CaptureImages' reply rather than
# from a streaming topic, so the pose it was captured at is unambiguous.
sensor_msgs/Image image

# Optional label carried through to the reply, e.g. a point id or a file name.
# Purely for the caller's own bookkeeping; inference ignores it.
string tag
---
bool success
string message

# The primary model's prediction — the slot inference_node lists first, which
# is by default the same graph the scan pipeline uses, so a UI reading only this
# field gets a number comparable with the scan CSVs. NaN when unavailable;
# callers must check, since success only means SOME slot produced a value.
float32 ra

# Every configured slot, in order. Parallel arrays: model_names[i] produced
# ra_values[i]. Kept generic rather than fixed fields because which models are
# worth comparing is a config decision that changes without a rebuild — a slot
# that failed to load appears here with NaN so the caller can see it was tried.
string[] model_names
float32[] ra_values

# Wall-clock seconds spent inside inference, excluding transport.
float32 elapsed_s

# Echoed back from the request.
string tag
